# Reproducible builds

<PROJECT> aims for [reproducible builds](https://reproducible-builds.org): anyone
should be able to rebuild a published binary from source and get **the same bytes**.

<!-- One or two sentences on WHY this matters for THIS project. The stronger the
trust requirement (wallets, networking, security tools), the more this matters.
Signed checksums prove *we* built a file; reproducibility lets *you* prove that
file is what the public source compiles to, with nothing added. -->

## Reproduce a release

```sh
git clone <CLONE-URL>
cd <PROJECT>
git checkout <TAG>            # the exact tag you are verifying

<REPRODUCE COMMAND>           # e.g. make reproduce
sha256sum <ARTIFACT>         # compare against the published SHA256SUMS
```

A matching SHA256 means your binary is byte-for-byte identical to the release.

## Verify determinism locally

```sh
<VERIFY COMMAND>             # e.g. make verify-repro — builds twice, compares hashes
```

## What is controlled

<!-- List every input that is pinned or normalized. Keep this honest and current. -->

| Input | How it's pinned |
|---|---|
| Toolchain | <e.g. GOTOOLCHAIN=go1.X.Y — a *stock* release, never locally patched> |
| Filesystem paths | <e.g. -trimpath / -ffile-prefix-map — no /home/you/... in the binary> |
| Build metadata | <e.g. -buildvcs=false, -buildid= — no dirty flag / build id> |
| Local env overrides | <e.g. GOENV=off, cleared CGO_* — no host paths baked in> |
| Dependencies | <e.g. go.sum / Cargo.lock / hashed lockfile — every dep pinned by hash> |
| Timestamps | `SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH` (the commit time) for any packaging step |
| Locale / timezone | `LC_ALL=C LANG=C TZ=UTC` |

